 #:seon.task{:name "a-step-var-defined-in-sci-cannot-be-built-into-a-proc"
             :plan "`seon.flow/var-process` refuses a step Var defined at an agent's REPL, so a flow test of a real proc step cannot be authored there. Repro (default caba650fa, agent chain-frictions-probe, 2026-10-10, SCI): (ns cf.scratch) (defn cf-step [state in] [state nil]) (seon.flow/var-process #'cf.scratch/cf-step :compute {:seon.env/environment {}}) answers \"refused argument 0 `step-var`: expected :seon.flow/step-var (must be a Var so a running graph hot reloads its step), got an instance of sci.lang.Var\" (the first call with two arguments is an arity refusal, a separate and correct answer). The `:seon.flow/step-var` schema accepts a host Var only, and `var-process` resolves it for hot reload; an SCI agent's definitions are program entities in its context. Done when a step Var the agent's context holds builds a launcher whose graph runs that definition (and hot reloads it), or the refusal names the supported way to test a step from the REPL, with a regression that defines a step in SCI and runs one proc step through `seon.flow/var-process`. Read `seon.flow/start-graph!` and `seon.sci.lookup/agent-test-namespace`."}
