             :plan "On a branch that changes `seon.cluster.source/proven-file`, its interpreted affected callers include the agent arming path, and `seon.turn.batch-test/a-repl-require-is-written-back-in-the-ns-form-and-reindexes-equal` and `seon.turn.batch-test/an-unchanged-committed-nilable-contract-is-admitted-and-written-back` go red under `my.test/check` with `seon.flow/var-process refused argument 0 step-var: ... got an instance of sci.lang.Var` (errors 3fac1c966cb6, 15e44d52d288); the same tests are green in a JVM loaded from the change (`my.test/check-platform`, 2026-10-10). A branch must never change the platform: compiled host-bound callers stay compiled. Done when a branch changing write-back runs those tests green on the branch. Read `seon.flow/var-process` and `seon.sci.eval/interpret-affected!`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-restart-starts-the-same-attempt-on-its-existing-branch"
             :plan "Phase H7 of the evidence (after H5, H6 and S3's `seon.task/attempt-tx`). `seon.flow/start-flow!` is the one path from an attempt row to a running or paused agent: request {task handle, agent id, branch, fork-point commit id, intent, graph?}; `seon.cluster.registry/fork!` (created? false on a repeat) -> `seon.cluster.store/open-branch!` -> `seon.turn.world/world` -> the one-fork environment (H5) -> `seon.flow/start-graph!` resumed only under :running (H6), registered in the registry under :seon.agent/started with its route and primed wake; graph? false answers the world alone (a test member). It folds in and deletes `seon.cluster.agent/start-flow!`, `seon.cluster.agent/start-claimed-flow!`, `seon.cluster.host/host!`, `seon.cluster.host/start!`, the per-branch db<->flow graph and the test-support launch helpers; `seon.flow/db<->flow` (R1) calls it. The task is read from main (its intent), the program from the branch; it renders nothing (the first turn's `seon.context/current-state` does). Measure first who reads :seon.agent/* from a branch value (`seon.cluster.host/close-admissions!`, `seon.cluster.host/retire!`) and convert them to main. Proofs: this test (a second start-flow! of an open attempt answers created? false, no second branch, the same agent id and graph); seon.cluster.agent-test/starting-one-agent-on-a-task-costs-under-a-second-and-300-mb tightened to attempt row -> first context under 150 ms and 40 MB warm through `seon.profile/measure` with the legs recorded as profile evidence (floor about 55 ms and 15 MB; now about 250 ms and 210 MB); seon.test-test/a-member-world-comes-from-start-flow-without-a-graph. Files: src/seon/flow.clj, src/seon/cluster/agent.clj, src/seon/cluster/host.clj, src/seon/test.clj, test/seon/cluster/agent_test.clj, test/seon/test_test.clj. Read `seon.sci.eval/base-ctx`, `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-11/hybrid-start-a-flow.md` and `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-11/r1-db-flow-design.md`."}
